es in their  career and so if they feel like they're  not getting what they need at a company  they're going to leave and that's  totally fine the best managers and  leaders totally get that if they don't  then  i think it can be kind of a toxic  environment so you should probably  reassess that and then my last hidden  secret which is related to kind of this  whole like if you are going to leave a  company then when you're going to look  for a new company then it's to look past  the curtains of hype and courtship at  any company to see what's really going  on this actually isn't limited to just  like looking for a new job but just like  in general this okay this is gonna sound  really pessimistic but people are really  good at marketing people are really good  at hyping things up in tech and you have  to like look past that and see what's  actually going on because especially for  engineers when we are really dealt with  dealing with the details and actually  executing on stuff we are where the  rubber hits the road and so if  recruiters are painting a rosy picture  of what it's like to work there or  managers are doing that i think it's  really important to be realistic about  like okay so like yes the company  culture and the company work-life  balance is awesome but where does it  suck and can i live with that and if a  company says they're changing the world  for things then like really kind of  think about it because i it's really  easy to appeal to that side to  individual contributors like the work  that you were doing is changing the  world but realistically is it though  like is it really changing the world or  is it changing this certain aspect of  things for these individual people in  certain use cases and what's actually  happening is gonna differ like based on  who you are and what your perspectives  are on the life in the world and stuff  but that's important to do you have to  understand what your values are and like  what you're willing to live with and not  live with so for instance if you're  interviewing a company you could ask  those existing employees what are the  challenges that you and your team are  facing right now some employees might  not be comfortable talking about that  which is totally fine because employees  sometimes don't want to like talk poorly  of their employer because the employer  has the power to fire that person  there's this whole kind of power  misbalance there so yeah don't fall for  the jargon don't fall for the marketing  it's good it has a purpose there's a  place there's a reason why you were able  to find that company because you  resonated with the message that's  getting put out but if you're really  thinking about what is going to be the  day-to-day or what it's like to work  with that person or you're going to work  on a project with them  be realistic all right so those are all  the hidden secrets of leading a tech  career from me to you hopefully that was  helpful i apologize if none of that made  sense but in my mind it does if you have  any hidden secrets for others or for me  then leave them in the comments down  below again one of the inspirations for  this video is just like seeing this in  day-to-day life when even in my work and  realizing what's helped me to get to  where i am and also helping others to  get to different parts of their career  as i've been kind of giving advice to  like individuals you all people through  my ios dev academy on what it takes to  become a successful software engineer  which yes success looks different and  means different things to different  people but i think there are some core  truths that allow you to like do the  work that you want to do no matter what  that work is a lot of it honestly is  just being a fun and good and easy  person to work with because everybody  likes to work with people who are easy  to work with and so hopefully these  skills will help you by the way this  codes pusher is limited edition so you  can pre